WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.060
There are plenty of Harry Potter fan theories
out there, but not all are created equal.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.660
From theories that solve minor plot holes
in the books to others that miss the mark

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.500
in bizarre ways, we've got some of the best
and some of the worst fan theories about everyone's

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:15.840
favorite teenage witch, Hermione Granger.

00:00:16.620 --> 00:00:21.400
If Hermione has one defining trait, it's her
extraordinary academic excellence. If you've

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:26.039
ever wondered why she excels so much, the
answer might be her Muggle upbringing. According

00:00:26.039 --> 00:00:31.099
to one fan theory, Hermione is such an excellent
student because she had more non-Hogwarts

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:34.880
schooling than most of her peers, and unlike
Harry, her family was supportive.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.620
"My parents are dentists."

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.180
Hermione would have attended Muggle school
until she was accepted into Hogwarts at age

00:00:42.190 --> 00:00:46.870
12. Learning about scientific theory and other
non-magical matters might have contributed

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:51.550
to a love of learning and helped her considerably
along the way. On the other hand, maybe she

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:53.360
just cares more than the other students?

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:58.620
"I'm going to bed before either of you come
up with another clever idea to get us killed,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:00.420
or worse, expelled."

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:04.920
It's pretty common for fan theories to take
something seemingly wholesome and twist it

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:09.560
into something dark and gritty. Although the
Harry Potter books get pretty grim themselves

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:13.600
in the last few installments, with numerous
beloved characters biting the magical bullet.

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:18.710
According to one fan theorist though, it was
actually even worse than it seemed. This idea

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:23.020
supposes that Hermione spent so much time
with Harry and Ron on their vacations because

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.980
she was homeless. Hermione allegedly saw the
writing on the wall that Voldemort was coming

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.399
back, so she erased her parents' minds in
advance and couch-surfed for her last three

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:33.400
years of school.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:38.000
Some of the best fan theories are the ones
that fill in small plot holes. When it comes

00:01:38.009 --> 00:01:42.280
to Harry Potter, there's arguably no other
plot development that's caused more headaches

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.540
than the Time Turner that Hermione uses in
Prisoner of Azkaban.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:50.340
Why the Ministry of Magic would let a student
harness time travel just to take more classes

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:56.040
is a baffling mystery. One fan theory offers
a convincing explanation: Hermione stole the

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:59.920
Time Turner from the Department of Mysteries,
possibly with Dumbledore's help.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.940
"You know the laws, Ms. Granger. You must
not be seen."

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:08.740
Fans love imagining that different characters
are actually the same character in different

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:13.170
stages of their life. It happened with Walter
White in Breaking Bad and Hal from Malcolm

00:02:13.170 --> 00:02:17.780
in the Middle, and it's happened with dozens
of other characters and actors. Usually, though,

00:02:17.780 --> 00:02:22.231
there's some common element that makes the
fan theory at least vaguely plausible. There's

00:02:22.231 --> 00:02:26.780
not much plausibility in the fan theory that
imagines that Matilda, from the classic Roald

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.440
Dahl story of the same name, is a young Hermione.

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:33.810
The theory seems to be based entirely on the
fact that both characters are young girls

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:38.761
with supernatural abilities and brunette hair.
There's not really much else to it, which

00:02:38.761 --> 00:02:42.560
makes it a pretty weak fan theory. If you
disagree, well:

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.740
"Listen you little wiseacre. I'm smart you're
dumb, I'm big you're little, I'm right and

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:50.980
you're wrong, and there's nothing you can
do about it."

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:56.020
In one popular fan theory, Hermione's cat,
Crookshanks, was actually the Potters' cat

00:02:56.020 --> 00:03:00.450
before Voldemort's attack. There are enough
clues in the text to make the theory work,

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.460
and it reassures cat lovers that the Potters'
old cat didn't just wander into the woods

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:10.011
to die. Most pertinently, it explains why
Crookshanks hated Ron's rat, Scabbers, it's

00:03:10.011 --> 00:03:14.340
because Crookshanks, as the Potters' former
cat, would have recognized Peter Pettigrew's

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:14.840
scent.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:19.720
The Harry Potter novels aren't exactly subtle
about the real-world parallels suggested by

00:03:19.730 --> 00:03:24.730
Muggle discrimination at Hogwarts. Draco Malfoy's
obsession with "pure-blooded" witches and

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:29.900
wizards unquestionably sets him up as a villain.
It's also no coincidence that Hermione, as

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:34.291
the series' most central Muggle-born witch,
is the smartest character in the books. It's

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:38.540
meant to highlight the inherent contradictions
of racism and other kinds of discrimination.

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:43.560
All of which is ruined by a fan theory that
imagines that Hermione isn't actually a Muggle-born

00:03:43.560 --> 00:03:48.750
witch at all. Supposedly, her family is descended
from a long line of witches and wizards, but

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.560
her parents are just Squibs (someone born
to magical parents without any magical powers

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:58.090
of their own). Sure, the theory explains why
Hermione shares a last name with a famous

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:02.760
wizard, but it also tears a hole in Hermione's
character and a fundamental message of the

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.760
books themselves.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:07.480
"You see Weasley, unlike some, my father can
afford the best."

00:04:08.160 --> 00:04:12.460
"At least no one on the Gryffindor team had
to buy their way in. They got in on pure talent."

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.120
Fans lost their minds with excitement when
a stage play sequel to the original books,

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:21.650
Harry Potter and the Cursed Child, was originally
announced. Unfortunately, some Harry Potter

00:04:21.650 --> 00:04:26.500
readers were upset when Noma Dumezweni, a
black actress, was cast to portray the older

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:31.560
Hermione for the stage. This led a number
of fans to point out that the book never actually

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:36.440
clarifies that Hermione isn't black. Although
the movies cast Emma Watson in the role, the

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:41.850
books never explicitly specify Hermione's
race. In fact, J. K. Rowling herself voiced

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.420
approval of Dumezweni's casting.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.520
Blame George Lucas for this one. Ever since
Luke and Leia were revealed to be twins in

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:53.250
Return of the Jedi, a secret sibling revelation
has become a constant source of fan theories

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:58.400
for just about everything. The reasoning behind
Hermione and Harry being secret siblings largely

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:02.691
boils down to the fact that the two characters
seem to have a close relationship... almost

00:05:02.691 --> 00:05:07.160
as if they were friends. Proponents of the
theory also argue that Lily and James could

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.900
possibly have had a secret child that they
put up for adoption. Considering that Rowling

00:05:11.900 --> 00:05:16.430
herself has admitted that maybe Harry and
Hermione should have gotten together romantically,

00:05:16.430 --> 00:05:19.060
this fan theory really doesn't hold up to
any scrutiny.

